  "question": {
    "text": "The charge/size ratio of a cation determines its polarizing power. Which one of the following sequences represents the increasing order of the polarizinig order of the polarizing power of the cationic species, $\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Be}^{2+}$ ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FDTjQ",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Be}^{2+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "l5S0v",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Be}^{2+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7frQ1",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{K}^{+}, \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Be}^{2+}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "mttmd",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}, \\mathrm{Be}^{2+}, \\mathrm{K}^{+}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Higher the charge/size ratio, more is the polarizing power.\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{K}^{+} < \\mathrm{Ca}^{2+} < \\mathrm{Mg}^{2+} < \\mathrm{Be}^{2+}$\nHence, (C) is correct.",
    "image": null
  },
